Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, adduser
Replaces: candled (<< 1.1.2), wincan-windows (<< 1.1.2)
Breaks: candled (<< 1.1.2), wincan-windows (<< 1.1.2)
Description: candle chart for the Windows desktop, and the Linux server that feeds it
 wincan is a Windows GUI and a Linux server to view your stock and crypto
 charts in real time, and see your win/loss as it happens.  This package has
 both halves.
 .
 candled, the server, serves candles as JSON over TLS.  It listens on the
 loopback address unless told otherwise and answers only the clients whose
 key it has been told, by the SHA-256 fingerprint of the client's own
 certificate (as an IRC bouncer does with certfp).  Its settings are in
 /etc/candled.conf; let a wincan in with "candled --authorize SHA256:...".
 .
 wincan.exe, the window, is a small frameless always-on-top candle chart for
 Windows, with a PowerShell installer, kept under /usr/share/wincan/windows
 for use from this system, for example under WSL2:
 .
  powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass \
    -File "$(wslpath -w /usr/share/wincan/windows/install.ps1)"
 .
 The Windows program is not run or used on Linux.
